    "turn_text": "let's talk about the other side of growth the issue of growth itself. I was reading something from Steve Moore earlier today, and he was pointing out stuff you and I have talked about before. We're worried on the national debt, which is about to accelerate from 100% of GDP to nearly 200% over the next 30 years, while the standard forecast from the CBO is predicated on the assumption of 1.7% annual economic growth. Way below the kinds of growth we've seen, oh, I don't know, throughout the 50s, 60s, 70s, 80s, 90s and early aughts. David, how are we ever going to get to 3.5%, 4% growth again? Not by the way, the right answer, the first right answer, I think you tell me if I'm wrong, is not doing what Bernie Sanders says.",
